<title>BELGIUM: Council to debate Internet child-sex porn controls.</title>
<headline>Council to debate Internet child-sex porn controls.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>At Belgium's request, the Telecommunications Council will debate on Friday ways to keep child-sex pornography off the Internet and other electronic networks.</p>
<p>The ministers are likely to ask the Commission to bring forward proposals as soon as possible, an Irish presidency source said.</p>
<p>He said licensing of Internet providers could be one way to deal with the problem.</p>
<p>Belgium is particularly concerned about paedophile pornography because of a child abduction, sex abuse and murder scandal.</p>
</text>
